+For the assay, reconstitute our lyophilized vaccine samples and standards in 600 µL of 9.0 g/L NaCl solution, then dilute them 1:1000 in 1X PBS / 0.05% Tween-20. Dispense samples and the standard curve in duplicate into the first column of a Greiner plate (cat. 655904), fill the remaining wells with sample diluent, and perform a 2.5-fold serial dilution. Prepare the bead mix by diluting each coupled bead set 1:10 in sample diluent, and add 10 µL of the mix to each well. Incubate the plate for 1 h at room temperature with 800 rpm agitation. Wash the plate three times with sample diluent using a magnetic washer. Add 100 µL of purified rabbit anti-CRM197 primary antiserum (Abcam ab53828, purified via Protein-G spin-trap) to each well and incubate under the same conditions. Wash three times, then add 50 µL of goat anti-rabbit IgG Fc-specific R-Phycoerythrin secondary antibody (Jackson ImmunoResearch 111-117-008, diluted 1:200) to each well. Incubate at room temperature with 800 rpm agitation. Wash the wells, resuspend in 100 µL of 1X PBS, agitate, and read on a Bio-Plex 200 instrument (high-sensitivity setting) using Bio-Plex Manager 6.0 software to record median fluorescence intensity. 
 
